  "narrative": {
    "intro": "National Steel and Shipbuilding has $2.8B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. National Steel and Shipbuilding has won 16 awards this fiscal year, and the average award size is $174M. National Steel and Shipbuilding obligations are up 406.3% year over year. Historical obligations show variability across recent fiscal years: FY21 was $471M, FY22 was $2.2B, FY23 was $1.2B, FY24 was $1.4B, and FY25 was $550M. National Steel and Shipbuilding current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date. National Steel and Shipbuilding concentration in large awards is evident from the average award size and the jump in obligations for FY26. National Steel and Shipbuilding performance this fiscal year will matter for suppliers, subcontractors, and competitors who track large-vessel and shipbuilding work. National Steel and Shipbuilding buyers and contracting officers should note the size and tempo of contracting activity when planning solicitations and oversight.",
